WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:05.040
Every knitter needs to understand
basic sweater styles.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:09.040
How do you choose what style
of sweater you want to knit?

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:12.000
There are so many sources of inspiration.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.120
You can comb your library of knitting
patterns,

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:19.720
maybe find a photo on the web or
in a store,

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.960
or maybe you've seen someone in a crowd
wearing a sweater that you love.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.200
Now, whether you chart your own sweaters,

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:33.240
use a knitwear design software program,
or you follow knitting patterns word

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:39.840
for word, it's valuable to understand
the various basic sweater shapes.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:42.560
If you're short on time or you're

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:47.520
an absolutely new knitter,
you probably want to choose an easier

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:51.800
style with the least amount
of shaping in the body and sleeves.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.680
Are you looking for a more tailored look?

00:00:54.760 --> 00:01:01.800
That means more shaping,
but the results are well worth the effort.

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:08.480
Let's use Penelope, the paper doll,
to examine some basic sweater styles.

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:16.920
By far, the easiest and quickest
style is the drop shoulder sweater.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.560
For a basic sweater, the only
shaping would be in the neckline.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:28.760
This style is great for oversized,
comfy, casual sweaters for adults.

00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:31.520
It's also for babies and kids.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.000
Really quick knitting.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:39.120
Now, the drawback of this style is there's
a lot of bulk at the underarm,

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.920
and it's not particularly
flattering for adult women.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.200
To eliminate the bulk and still have

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:53.600
a fast and easy shape to knit,
there is the modified drop shoulder style.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.360
It's also called a square arm hole.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:58.360
You bind off a few stitches

00:01:58.440 --> 00:02:02.200
at the underarm, you change the sleeve
shaping a little bit,

00:02:02.280 --> 00:02:09.280
and again, you have a very casual style,
and the knitting is still quick and easy.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:12.680
You'll often see men's
sweaters knit in this style.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:16.400
It gives lots of room in the arm hole.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:18.680
The modified drop shoulder also

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:22.120
accommodates a large
range of shoulder widths.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.160
So if you're knitting for someone and you

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:28.400
don't have all of their specific
measurements, this style is perfect.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:33.520
It isn't critical where
the shoulder seam falls.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:37.800
The most tailored style
is the set-in sleeve.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:41.200
This is the classic shape for sweaters.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:43.640
The shoulder seam should be precisely

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:47.120
placed according to the
wearer's shoulder width.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:52.440
The curved underarm also adds
to the fit of this style.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:55.360
The set-in sleeve cap eliminates extra

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:02.320
bulk on the top of the sleeve
and offers a more fitted appearance.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.120
Now, this style has the most shaping when

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.960
knitting,
and sadly, many knitters avoid set

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:12.760
in sleeves,
but the extra time to shape the arm hole

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:17.000
in the sleeve cap is well worth
the professional appearance

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:22.200
and the appealing silhouette
of the finished garment.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:25.720
Here's another easy to knit sweater shape.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.400
It's the raglin' sleeve.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.320
Now, the straight line decolour creases
when knitting this,

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:36.480
they're really easy to knit and they offer
you an opportunity to add stitch detail

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:41.600
along the seam for a really
personalized sweater.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:45.960
Many knitters will knit ragged
and sleeve sweaters from the up, down.

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:53.600
Now, this adds to the speed of knitting
by joining the pieces as you knit,

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:59.720
and it also offers a break
from our usual hem up construction.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:04.480
Like drop shoulder styles,
raglins can accommodate a wide variety

00:04:04.560 --> 00:04:11.560
of shoulder widths, making them
versatile for babies, kids, and adults.

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.720
Train yourself to recognize the basic

00:04:15.800 --> 00:04:21.040
sweater shapes when looking at ready-made
garments or knitting patterns.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.960
This will help you determine if
the pattern is right for your next project

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:32.680
based on your skills and the time you want
to devote to the finishing the sweater.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:35.280
Now, machine knitters often complain

00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:39.640
that there aren't updated machine
knitting patterns available.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:42.040
Here's my challenge to you.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:48.160
First, learn to translate hand
knitting patterns to machine knitting.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:54.760
Second, chart your own patterns
from styles that you've seen.

00:04:54.840 --> 00:05:02.760
And finally, if you use knitting software,
practice it and master it.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:07.760
Arm with this knowledge and some practice,

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:12.680
soon you'll find that the sky's the limit,
and you'll be knitting all of those

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:18.160
beautiful designs that are
rolling around in your head.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:20.000
Knit it now has more resources about

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:23.040
knitwear design, along
with many other topics.

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:25.000
Please consider becoming a member,

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:29.040
and let us help you become
a better machine knitter.

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:29.880
Happy knitting.

